      "excerpt": "A stock listed in kroner or yen hides a risk the numbers don't show directly: currency risk. Here's how I handle it.",
      "metaDescription": "How currency risk affects an investor buying foreign stocks listed in local currency. Real examples: Kongsberg, Advantest, TCS.",
      "answer": "A stock listed in Norwegian krone, Japanese yen, or Indian rupee exposes a foreign investor to an additional risk, independent of the company's performance: the exchange rate movement between that currency and their own. Even an excellent stock can become a bad investment if the local currency collapses.",
