      answer: "Alphabet posted record revenue of $119.8 billion in Q2 2026, up 24%, with cloud accelerating to +82%. Yet the stock barely moved: the company also just raised its 2026 capex budget to $190 billion, sharply compressing available cash. Here is how I separate the real acceleration from the real risk.",
